<h2>NPC stat block</h2>
<p>The narrative form a Dream Master reads aloud: <code>@npc-stat</code> with a <code>####</code> name, a <code>&gt;</code> flavor line, the stat lines, and <code>#####</code> sub-headings for traits and equipment.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="593:613" class="language-markdown">@npc-stat

#### Patchhead

&gt; See a Patchhead comin' at you, you best move. Ain't no reasoning with 'em.

2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Usually Small to Medium

##### Traits

**Bloodlust:** Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.

##### Equipment

Weighted chains, shivs, knuckle dusters; junk shields or crash helmets.

@end-npc-stat
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="section dc-section-panel dc-npc-stat" data-source-range="618:619"><h4>Patchhead</h4>
<blockquote>
<p data-source-range="622:623">See a Patchhead comin’ at you, you best move. Ain’t no reasoning with 'em.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Usually Small to Medium</p>
<h5>Traits</h5>
<p><strong>Bloodlust:</strong> Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.</p>
<h5>Equipment</h5>
<p>Weighted chains, shivs, knuckle dusters; junk shields or crash helmets.</p>
</div></div>
<p>A block with several <code>####</code> entries breaks between creatures and never inside one; the title bar stays with the first entry. A block with no <code>####</code> is one creature; add <code>.dc-avoid-split</code> (<code>@npc-stat .dc-avoid-split</code>) to keep it on one page.</p>
<p>To set the entries in columns, put them in <code>@columns 2</code> inside the block: the bar and an optional intro stay above, full width.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="643:678" class="language-markdown">@npc-stat

### Street Crews

Two crews that work the same block.

@columns 2

#### Patchhead

&gt; See a Patchhead comin' at you, you best move.

2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Small to Medium

##### Traits

**Bloodlust:** Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.

#### Grease Monkey

&gt; Hold still, this'll only sting a lot.

3 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Medium

##### Traits

**Quick Fix:** A Grease Monkey patches an ally for 1 HP once per scene.

@end-columns

@end-npc-stat
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="section dc-section-panel dc-npc-stat" data-source-range="683:684"><h3>Street Crews</h3>
<p>Two crews that work the same block.</p>
<div class="gp-columns gp-columns-2" data-columns="2" data-source-range="689:690"><h4>Patchhead</h4>
<blockquote>
<p data-source-range="693:694">See a Patchhead comin’ at you, you best move.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Small to Medium</p>
<h5>Traits</h5>
<p><strong>Bloodlust:</strong> Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.</p>
<h4>Grease Monkey</h4>
<blockquote>
<p data-source-range="704:705">Hold still, this’ll only sting a lot.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>3 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Medium</p>
<h5>Traits</h5>
<p><strong>Quick Fix:</strong> A Grease Monkey patches an ally for 1 HP once per scene.</p>
</div></div></div>
<p>Tokens: <code>--dc-npc-stat-label-color</code>, <code>--dc-npc-stat-primary</code>, <code>--dc-npc-stat-secondary</code>, <code>--dc-npc-stat-rule</code>, <code>--dc-npc-stat-rule-width</code>.</p>
<h2>Stat grid and at-a-glance cards</h2>
<p>Two raw-HTML forms for numbers at a glance. The four-cell stat grid takes combat stats (HP / DEF / AP / DMG) for a creature or social stats (REP / HEAT / FEE / TURN) for a contact; the at-a-glance row is one label and one value per card.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="725:748" class="language-markdown">&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat dc-flush&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-head&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-name&quot;&gt;Doc Solenn&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-class&quot;&gt;— Contact · Ripperdoc —&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-grid&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-key&quot;&gt;REP&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-val&quot;&gt;4&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-key&quot;&gt;HEAT&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-val&quot;&gt;2&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-key&quot;&gt;FEE&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-val&quot;&gt;×1.5&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-key&quot;&gt;TURN&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-cell-val&quot;&gt;−1&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;dc-stat-line&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patch Job:&lt;/strong&gt; treats wounds between scenes for FEE × severity.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

@columns 3

&lt;div class=&quot;dc-at-a-glance-card&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;HP&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;14&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dc-at-a-glance-card&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Speed&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Near&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dc-at-a-glance-card&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Heat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;3&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

@end-columns
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="dc-stat dc-flush">
  <div class="dc-stat-head">
    <div class="dc-stat-name">Doc Solenn</div>
    <div class="dc-stat-class">— Contact · Ripperdoc —</div>
  </div>
  <div class="dc-stat-grid">
    <div class="dc-stat-cell"><div class="dc-stat-cell-key">REP</div><div class="dc-stat-cell-val">4</div></div>
    <div class="dc-stat-cell"><div class="dc-stat-cell-key">HEAT</div><div class="dc-stat-cell-val">2</div></div>
    <div class="dc-stat-cell"><div class="dc-stat-cell-key">FEE</div><div class="dc-stat-cell-val">×1.5</div></div>
    <div class="dc-stat-cell"><div class="dc-stat-cell-key">TURN</div><div class="dc-stat-cell-val">−1</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="dc-stat-line"><strong>Patch Job:</strong> treats wounds between scenes for FEE × severity.</div>
</div>
<div class="gp-columns gp-columns-3" data-columns="3" data-source-range="767:768"><div class="dc-at-a-glance-card"><h4>HP</h4><p>14</p></div>
<div class="dc-at-a-glance-card"><h4>Speed</h4><p>Near</p></div>
<div class="dc-at-a-glance-card"><h4>Heat</h4><p>3</p></div>
</div></div>
<h2>NPC sidebar</h2>
<p>A contact capsule floated beside prose: a <code>.dc-human-callout</code> inside a raw <code>.dc-sidebar</code>.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="781:787" class="language-markdown">&lt;div class=&quot;dc-sidebar&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-human-callout&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vance &quot;Static&quot; Oyelaran&lt;/strong&gt; — Fixer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two cybernetic eyes, owes everyone. &lt;strong&gt;Hook:&lt;/strong&gt; the chip is real; the access tunnel on it is bait.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage dg-on-paper">
<p>The Dreamers are low on credits and lower on luck when the noodle-stall door swings open. A figure slides into the booth across from them, drops a battered data chip on the table, and waits.</p>
<div class="dc-sidebar"><div class="dc-human-callout">
<p><strong>Vance "Static" Oyelaran</strong> — Fixer</p>
<p>Two cybernetic eyes, owes everyone. <strong>Hook:</strong> the chip is real; the access tunnel on it is bait.</p>
</div></div>
<p>Read the room before you read the chip. A fixer who makes it back out the door clean is a fixer who knew the drone was coming. Either way, the job’s already in motion the moment Static sat down.</p>
</div>
</div></div>"
`;

exports[`rendered output 07-specialty-system.md matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"<div class="chapter dg-guide" id="ch-specialty" data-ch="7" data-source-range="0:1"><div class="page dg-doc chapter-7" data-source-range="2:3"><p class="dg-kicker">Chapter 7</p>
<h1>The Specialty System</h1>
<p class="dg-lede">The richest family in the book. A specialty wrapper sets the shape and color; inside it, an intro panel, an art plate, a catalog card, learning paths, and skill cards all inherit that identity. Authors never set a variant on a card — the parent decides.</p>
<h2>Specialty</h2>
<p><code>@specialty .&lt;name&gt;</code> is the parent scope. It emits nothing visible itself; every component inside it reads its clip-path silhouettes and accent color. Ten families ship:</p>
<p><code>augmerc</code> · <code>proxy</code> · <code>streetwarden</code> · <code>gutterdruid</code> · <code>cybersurgeon</code> · <code>wirephreak</code> · <code>technosorcerer</code> · <code>etherlock</code> · <code>dualist</code> · <code>generalist</code></p>
<pre><code data-source-range="17:24" class="language-markdown">@specialty .augmerc

… intro, art, learning paths, skills …

@end-specialty
</code></pre>
<p>Opening a new <code>@specialty</code> closes the previous one, along with every path and skill inside it. <code>@end-specialty</code> does the same, and so does the next <code>@chapter</code>, <code>@page</code> or <code>@section</code>: a specialty cannot straddle a page, so put a page break inside one with <code>@page-break</code>. A specialty is written one of two ways, <code>@specialty augmerc</code> or <code>@specialty .augmerc</code>, and both give the same wrapper. A skill belongs inside a learning path inside a specialty; the Problems panel flags a skill sitting directly in the specialty. Tokens the wrapper sets for its children: <code>--spec-accent</code>, <code>--spec-mid</code>, <code>--spec-dark</code>, <code>--dc-skill-tab-shape</code>, <code>--dc-skill-body-shape</code>, <code>--dc-path-title-shape</code>, <code>--dc-path-shell-clip</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-card-shell-shape</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-title-shape</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-clip</code>.</p>
<h2>Specialty intro</h2>
<p>The title-banded panel on a specialty’s first page: the <code>##</code> name, the pitch, and a <code>###</code> spec tweak.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="31:48" class="language-markdown">@specialty .augmerc

@specialty-intro

## Augmerc

An Augmerc is muscle for hire. Street thugs, corporate bodyguards, deniable enforcers — the difference is gear, grafts, and how much of them is still original.

### Spec Tweak: **Wired to Kill**

Augmerc learning paths assume combat-grade augmentations. Without the implants, the Augmerc spends 1 extra AP to activate a path's abilities.

@end-specialty-intro

@end-specialty
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="dc-specialty augmerc" data-source-range="53:54"><div class="dc-specialty-intro" data-source-range="55:56"><h2>Augmerc</h2>
<p>An Augmerc is muscle for hire. Street thugs, corporate bodyguards, deniable enforcers — the difference is gear, grafts, and how much of them is still original.</p>
<h3>Spec Tweak: <strong>Wired to Kill</strong></h3>
<p>Augmerc learning paths assume combat-grade augmentations. Without the implants, the Augmerc spends 1 extra AP to activate a path’s abilities.</p>
</div></div></div>
<p>Tokens: <code>--dc-specialty-intro-bg</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-title-bg</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-title-color</code>.</p>
<h2>Specialty art</h2>
<p>A full-page art plate. It takes its own page and bleeds to the edge; in a book this follows the intro. The rendered plate is the next page.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="77:88" class="language-markdown">@specialty .augmerc

@specialty-art

![Augmerc](https://placehold.co/640x360/1a1d2b/e8503a/png?text=Augmerc)

@end-specialty-art

@end-specialty
</code></pre>
<div class="dc-specialty augmerc" data-source-range="89:90"><div class="dc-specialty-art" data-source-range="91:92"><p class="dc-img-wrapper"><img src="https://placehold.co/640x360/1a1d2b/e8503a/png?text=Augmerc" alt="Augmerc" data-gp-source-token="![Augmerc](https://placehold.co/640x360/1a1d2b/e8503a/png?text=Augmerc)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0"></p>
</div></div><h2>Specialty card</h2>
<p>The catalog card for a “choose your specialty” page: portrait, a <code>&gt;</code> tagline, and a short pitch, inside a <code>@card-grid</code>, with <code>@columns 2</code> laying the cards out two across. Each card sits in its own <code>@specialty</code> so it carries its own color.</p>
<pre><code class="dg-split language-markdown" data-source-range="104:145">@card-grid

@columns 2

@specialty .augmerc

@specialty-card #card-augmerc

### Augmerc

![Augmerc](https://placehold.co/300x340/1a1d2b/e8503a/png?text=Augmerc)

&gt; Cybernetic Commando

Heavily armed and wired for war, Augmercs are the blunt force of any squad.

@end-specialty-card

@end-specialty

@specialty .gutterdruid

@specialty-card #card-gutterdruid

### Gutterdruid

![Gutterdruid](https://placehold.co/300x340/1a1d2b/4a9d6e/png?text=Gutterdruid)

&gt; Feral Shapeshifter

Gutterdruids rewrite their own flesh to match the wasteland around them.

@end-specialty-card

@end-specialty

@end-columns

@end-card-grid
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="section dc-card-grid" data-source-range="150:151"><div class="gp-columns gp-columns-2" data-columns="2" data-source-range="152:153"><div class="dc-specialty augmerc" data-source-range="154:155"><div class="dc-specialty-card" id="card-augmerc" data-position="odd" data-source-range="156:157"><h3>Augmerc</h3>
<p class="dc-img-wrapper"><img src="https://placehold.co/300x340/1a1d2b/e8503a/png?text=Augmerc" alt="Augmerc" data-gp-source-token="![Augmerc](https://placehold.co/300x340/1a1d2b/e8503a/png?text=Augmerc)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0"></p>
